{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>they will lick, etc., all our surroundings.</b> Perhaps they did not wish to show so much faintness of heart that they were afraid of them, but rather that they were concerned for the surrounding peoples, and they spoke in plural language to include them with themselves. And the statement <b>and Balak son of Zippor</b> — these are the words of Scripture; or it is possible that these are their own words, which they said because this matter touches Midian as well, since Balak son of Zippor was king of Moab at that time, and if so the disgrace touches Midian on account of their prince. And Scripture was precise in saying <b>at that time</b>, to say: not before it and not after it, for after Balaam came and informed them that they would not harm or destroy Moab, they deposed Balak and he was no longer king over them. And this is your sign: he is found with the princes of Midian and was killed with them (Numbers 31:8)."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:11:55.656918753Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}